      "id": "antony-and-cleopatra/sceneIII_3.11/p@126590",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "ANTONY.\nHark, the land bids me tread no more upon’t.\nIt is ashamed to bear me. Friends, come hither.\nI am so lated in the world that I\nHave lost my way for ever. I have a ship\nLaden with gold. Take that, divide it. Fly,\nAnd make your peace with Caesar.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
